    "title": "CBP Intercepts Vessel Carrying 17 Near San Clemente Island, Transfers Individuals to Local Border Patrol - NewsBreak",
    "text": "3 hours ago On November 19, 2025, U.S. Customs and Border Protection's Air and Marine Operations, with help from the U.S. Navy, intercepted a panga-style vessel near San Clemente Island, off the coast of San Diego. The vessel carried 17 people. Sailors aboard the USS Sampson first detected the boat. Marine Interdiction Agents responded and apprehended the group. All individuals said they were Mexican citizens. The incident happened at about 2:40 a.m. The individuals were later transferred to San Clemente Border Patrol agents for processing.\nCBP stated that it works with other agencies to address smuggling and enforce border laws. The agency said it continues to monitor and protect U.S. borders on land, air, and sea.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.\n4",
